/favicon-192.png\" />\n\n  <!-- 57x57 (precomposed) for iPhone 3GS, pre-2011 iPod Touch and older Android devices -->\n  <link rel=\"apple-touch-icon-precomposed\" href=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/coreutils/nwds/img/favicons/favicon-57.png\">\n  <!-- 72x72 (precomposed) for 1st generation iPad, iPad 2 and iPad mini -->\n  <link rel=\"apple-touch-icon-precomposed\" sizes=\"72x72\" href=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/coreutils/nwds/img/favicons/favicon-72.png\">\n  <!-- 114x114 (precomposed) for iPhone 4, 4S, 5 and post-2011 iPod Touch -->\n  <link rel=\"apple-touch-icon-precomposed\" sizes=\"114x114\" href=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/coreutils/nwds/img/favicons/favicon-114.png\">\n  <!-- 144x144 (precomposed) for iPad 3rd and 4th generation -->\n  <link rel=\"apple-touch-icon-precomposed\" sizes=\"144x144\" href=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/coreutils/nwds/img/favicons/favicon-144.png\">\n\n\n  <!-- For Pinger + Google Optimize integration (NS-820) -->\n  <meta name=\"ncbi_sg_optimize_id\" content=\"\">\n\n  <!-- Mobile browser address bar color -->\n  <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#20558a\">\n\n  <!-- Preserve the Referrer when going from HTTPS to HTTP -->\n  <meta name=\"referrer\" content=\"origin-when-cross-origin\">\n\n  <meta name=\"ncbi_pinger_gtm_track\" content=\"true\"/>\n<!-- Logging params: Pinger defaults -->\n\n  \n    <meta name=\"ncbi_app\" content=\"pubmed\" />\n  \n\n  \n    <meta name=\"ncbi_db\" content=\"pubmed\" />\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n    <meta name=\"ncbi_phid\" content=\"F804000195D1CEB500003D63BD3E3CAE.1.m_2\" />\n  \n\n  \n    <meta name=\"ncbi_pinger_stat_url\" content=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/stat\" />\n  \n\n  \n    <meta name=\"log_category\" content=\"literature\" />\n  \n\n  \n    <meta name=\"ncbi_cost_center\" content=\"pubmed\" />\n  \n\n\n\n  <!-- Logging params: Pinger custom -->\n  \n    <meta name=\"ncbi_pdid\" content=\"pubmed\" />\n  \n    <meta name=\"log_op\" content=\"retrieve\" />\n  \n    <meta name=\"uid\" content=\"31609649\" />\n  \n    <meta name=\"ncbi_uid\" content=\"31609649\" />\n  \n\n\n\n  <!-- Social meta tags for unfurling urls -->\n  \n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"31609649\"><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index,nofollow,noarchive\"><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"31609649\"><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31609649/?format=pubmed\"><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"31609649\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/persistent/pubmed-meta-image-v2.jpg\"><meta property=\"og:image:secure_url\" content=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/persistent/pubmed-meta-image-v2.jpg\"><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\"><meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"PubMed\"><meta name=\"twitter:domain\" content=\"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\"><meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"31609649\"><meta name=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31609649/?format=pubmed\"><meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"31609649\"><meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/persistent/pubmed-meta-image-v2.jpg\">\n\n\n  <!-- OpenSearch XML -->\n  <link rel=\"search\" type=\"application/opensearchdescription+xml\" href=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/persistent/opensearch.xml\" title=\"PubMed search\">\n\n  <!-- Disables severely broken elements when no JS -->\n  <noscript>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/a2ffdabe-e220-486a-83d1-09afbe4369a3/core/no-script.css\">\n  </noscript>\n\n  \n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31609649/?format=pubmed\" />\n  \n\n\n</head>\n<body >\n\n  \n  <div class=\"article-page\" id=\"article-page\">\n    \n      <pre class=\"article-details\" id=\"article-details\">PMID- 31609649\r\nOWN - NLM\r\nSTAT- MEDLINE\r\nDCOM- 20200626\r\nLR  - 20221207\r\nIS  - 1527-7755 (Electronic)\r\nIS  - 0732-183X (Print)\r\nIS  - 0732-183X (Linking)\r\nVI  - 38\r\nIP  - 1\r\nDP  - 2020 Jan 1\r\nTI  - Germline GPR161 Mutations Predispose to Pediatric Medulloblastoma.\r\nPG  - 43-50\r\nLID - 10.1200/JCO.19.00577 [doi]\r\nAB  - PURPOSE: The identification of a heritable tumor predisposition often leads to \r\n      changes in management and increased surveillance of individuals who are at risk; \r\n      however, for many rare entities, our knowledge of heritable predisposition is \r\n      incomplete. METHODS: Families with childhood medulloblastoma, one of the most \r\n      prevalent childhood malignant brain tumors, were investigated to identify \r\n      predisposing germline mutations. Initial findings were extended to genomes and \r\n      epigenomes of 1,044 medulloblastoma cases from international multicenter cohorts, \r\n      including retrospective and prospective clinical studies and patient series. \r\n      RESULTS: We identified heterozygous germline mutations in the G protein-coupled \r\n      receptor 161 (GPR161) gene in six patients with infant-onset medulloblastoma \r\n      (median age, 1.5 years). GPR161 mutations were exclusively associated with the \r\n      sonic hedgehog medulloblastoma (MB(SHH)) subgroup and accounted for 5% of infant \r\n      MB(SHH) cases in our cohorts. Molecular tumor profiling revealed a loss of \r\n      heterozygosity at GPR161 in all affected MB(SHH) tumors, atypical somatic copy \r\n      number landscapes, and no additional somatic driver events. Analysis of 226 \r\n      MB(SHH) tumors revealed somatic copy-neutral loss of heterozygosity of chromosome \r\n      1q as the hallmark characteristic of GPR161 deficiency and the primary mechanism \r\n      for biallelic inactivation of GPR161 in affected MB(SHH) tumors. CONCLUSION: \r\n      Here, we describe a novel brain tumor predisposition syndrome that is caused by \r\n      germline GPR161 mutations and characterized by MB(SHH) in infants. Additional \r\n      studies are needed to identify a potential broader tumor spectrum associated with \r\n      germline GPR161 mutations.\r\nFAU - Begemann, Matthias\r\nAU  - Begemann M\r\nAD  - RWTH Aachen University, Aachen, Germany.\r\nFAU - Waszak, Sebastian M\r\nAU  - Waszak SM\r\nAD  - European Molecular Biology Laboratory, Heidelberg, Germany.\r\nFAU - Robinson, Giles W\r\nAU  - Robinson GW\r\nAD  - St Jude Children&#x27;s Research Hospital, Memphis, TN.\r\nFAU - Jäger, Natalie\r\nAU  - Jäger N\r\nAD  - Hopp Children&#x27;s Cancer Center Heidelberg, Heidelberg, Germany.\r\nAD  - German Cancer Research Centre, Heidelberg, Germany.\r\nFAU - Sharma, Tanvi\r\nAU  - Sharma T\r\nAD  - Hopp Children&#x27;s Cancer Center Heidelberg, Heidelberg, Germany.\r\nAD  - German Cancer Research Centre, Heidelberg, Germany.\r\nFAU - Knopp, Cordula\r\nAU  - Knopp C\r\nAD  - RWTH Aachen University, Aachen, Germany.\r\nFAU - Kraft, Florian\r\nAU  - Kraft F\r\nAD  - RWTH Aachen University, Aachen, Germany.\r\nFAU - Moser, Olga\r\nAU  - Moser O\r\nAD  - RWTH Aachen University, Aachen, Germany.\r\nFAU - Mynarek, Martin\r\nAU  - Mynarek M\r\nAD  - University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf, Hamburg, Germany.\r\nFAU - Guerrini-Rousseau, Lea\r\nAU  - Guerrini-Rousseau L\r\nAD  - Gustave Roussy Cancer Center, Villejuif, Paris, France.\r\nFAU - Brugieres, Laurence\r\nAU  - Brugieres L\r\nAD  - Gustave Roussy Cancer Center, Villejuif, Paris, France.\r\nFAU - Varlet, Pascale\r\nAU  - Varlet P\r\nAD  - Université Paris Descartes, Paris, France.\r\nFAU - Pietsch, Torsten\r\nAU  - Pietsch T\r\nAD  - University of Bonn, Bonn, Germany.\r\nFAU - Bowers, Daniel C\r\nAU  - Bowers DC\r\nAD  - University of Texas Southwestern Medical School, Dallas, TX.\r\nFAU - Chintagumpala, Murali\r\nAU  - Chintagumpala M\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
